# Facts about Old Pell.

@fact pell.apothecary
tier: surface
text: Runs the drawers at Pell & Daughters. He taught three generations of the village to count drops.

@fact pell.counting
tier: personal
hint: Take the Apothecary Clerk job.
unlock: seen(pell_count_drops) > 0
text: He makes every new clerk count aloud. He trusts people who measure twice.

@fact pell.daughters
tier: personal
hint: Work for him as his clerk, and work well.
unlock: seen(pell_daughters) > 0
text: His daughters run the counter and want the shop to change; he wants it to be fifty years ago. They're all secretly proud of each other.

@fact pell.spoon
tier: personal
hint: Visit Pell & Daughters in your second year.
unlock: seen(offer_measuring_spoon) > 0
text: His brass measuring spoon hasn't been wrong in forty years. His daughters learned to measure on it, and say it's theirs.

@fact pell.oldest_drawer
tier: personal
hint: Work as his clerk until you are promoted.
unlock: seen(pell_oldest_drawer) > 0
text: His oldest drawer holds a yellowed card for a draught "of your own strength", in a hand older than his. He has labelled it "Not yet."

@fact pell.humming
tier: personal
hint: Visit Pell & Daughters.
unlock: seen(pell_apothecary_humming_drawer) > 0
text: Some of his thousand drawers hum. He relabels them himself, in a precise hand: ASK FIRST, NOT TODAY.
